    "body": "> It would also be nice to have a declarative API for this, e.g.\r\n> \r\n> ```\r\n> @view-transition {\r\n>   navigation: auto;\r\n>   has-ua-visual-transition: skip;\r\n> }\r\n> ```\r\n\r\n\r\nThis feels like a side-ask to the feature being asked here.\r\n\r\n- What this issue is about: a way to _detect_ whether a UA Visual Transition was provided in order to skip your own transition.\r\n- What you are asking: a way to _prevent_ (and maybe later even hijack) the UA-provided Visual Transition\r\n\r\nThe latter is being discussed in https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/8747\r\n",
