    "updated_at": "2025-01-28T15:30:23Z",
    "body": "I can't come up with one offhand. Perhaps an animation that should play on the new page but presumably the UA transition already shows the fully rendered new state, or renders it directly. \n\nPerhaps it's enough to just default to skipping cross-doc transitions when there is a UA visual transition. Anything more than that would involve something more advanced that doesn't yet exist, like gesture-linked cross-doc VTs and that would have its own details to work out. ",
