    "body": "> Is there any conceivable use cases in which you _would_ want to run both transitions?\n\nYes, but then authors might want to change the animations.\n\n- No `hasUAVisualTransition`? Perform a slide animation\n- Has `hasUAVisualTransition`? Do a slight grow+fade-in animation\n\n> Shouldn't the UA _always_ skip the cross-document view transition in this scenario?\n\nSee above :)\n\nAlso, by having `hasUAVisualTransition` on cross-document transitions, the way authors approach things would be consistent between same-doc and cross-doc: _“Check the `hasUAVisualTransition` value”_.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
