    "created_at": "2025-09-05T10:58:26Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-09-05T11:05:51Z",
    "body": "> * Has `hasUAVisualTransition`? Do a slight grow+fade-in animation\n\nWouldn't this still look really weird?\n\nI agree with @noamr that it should always skip/avoid the transition. Places where both are acceptable seems like the edge case, and in those cases we can add a declarative opt in:\n\n```css\n@view-transition {\n  navigation: auto;\n  even-if-the-ua-did-its-own-transition: im-serious;\n}\n```\n\nand in that case we'd need `hasUAVisualTransition` somewhere in JS, or as a CSS pseudo class.",
