    "created_at": "2025-09-16T13:10:36Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-09-16T13:11:06Z",
    "body": "@bramus \n\n> If we do skip by default, my fear is that authors won’t include a `hasUAVisualTransition` check for cross-doc navigations and get used to that. And when they later do opt-in after all, then they suddenly need to add the check after all\n\nIt seems odd to add code to opt-into a specific thing, then not add code to handle that specific thing, no?\n\nIt seems much more likely to forget to handle `hasUAVisualTransition` on `NavigationActivation` because you didn't know it, or UA transitions were a thing.\n\nThe opt-in exists for cases where you want to perform a transition despite there already being a UA transition, which feels really edge-casey, and should be handled with care.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
