    "body": "> I’m not gonna die on this hill so I’m fine with auto-skipping the cross-doc VT in case there is UA transition happening :)\n> \n> So how do we move this one forward? I’m seeing:\n> \n> 1. Add `hasUAVisualTransition` to the HTML spec.\n\nWhat does that buy you on top of checking `pageRevealEvent.viewTransition` ?\n\n> 3. File issue at the CSSWG to auto-skip the Cross-Doc VT in case there was a UA transition\n\nThat's already in the spec:\nhttps://drafts.csswg.org/css-view-transitions-2/#navigation-can-trigger-a-cross-document-view-transition:~:text=the%20user%20agent%20may%20ignore%20the%20author%2Ddefined%20view%20transition\n\n> 4. File follow-up at the CSSWG to give authors a way to not skip the Cross-Doc VT after all (+ stretch goal: to override the default UA transition with their own transition)> \n> I can do 2 + 3 _(and already have a worked out a proposal for 3 in my head)_, but am not familiar with the process to getting 1 on the agenda here.\n\n",
