    "updated_at": "2025-10-22T08:57:07Z",
    "body": "> > I’m not gonna die on this hill so I’m fine with auto-skipping the cross-doc VT in case there is UA transition happening :)\n> > So how do we move this one forward? I’m seeing:\n> > \n> > 1. Add `hasUAVisualTransition` to the HTML spec.\n> \n> What does that buy you on top of checking `pageRevealEvent.viewTransition` ?\n\nThey check two different things. Especially with the current wording being _“the UA **may** ignore”_, the two are not opposites of each other.\n\n> > 2. File issue at the CSSWG to auto-skip the Cross-Doc VT in case there was a UA transition\n> \n> That's already in the spec: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-view-transitions-2/#navigation-can-trigger-a-cross-document-view-transition:~:text=the%20user%20agent%20may%20ignore%20the%20author%2Ddefined%20view%20transition\n\nI’m fine with leaving this as is then, but it definitely makes 1 very much necessary.\n\n",
