    "created_at": "2026-05-28T18:54:32Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-05-28T18:54:32Z",
    "body": "I was pointed to this issue because I noticed the same thing when trying to add FLIP transitions to an Astro site, which neither as a MPA nor a SPA can feature them due to UA transition handlers. \n\nIn my eyes this begs the question of why (especially named) transitions were adopted in the first place, if the two big browser engines choose to override them.\n\nThis becomes especially frustrating when aiming for a CSS only approach — adding JS to disable a baseline feature, to have less intentional transitions, because browser vendors chose to override the platform.",
